    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "description": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "No data",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [],
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Active decision ≠ blocked request.** A scenario trigger may only produce a simulated alert. Cowrie is configured for immediate decisions; the tarpit scenario is simulated. Traefik applies IP decisions to protected HTTP services; Cowrie remains accessible.\n\nThe tables below show **current local/manual enforcement decisions**, refreshed within roughly 60 seconds. Empty rows are meaningful only when **Decision inventory = CURRENT**. Open **Active decisions · local UI** for management and **CrowdSec Console** for cloud reporting."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Who has a decision · expiry and recent observations",
      "type": "row",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8,
